        "Gross-Up provisions matter most in NNN and Modified Gross commercial Leases. Variable Operating Expenses (utilities, janitorial, supplies) drop when a building runs partly vacant — but Tenants paying pro-rata shares would see those drops as savings. Gross-Up adjusts variable expenses upward to what they'd be at the gross-up occupancy (typically 95-100%), then allocates the grossed-up amount pro-rata. Without Gross-Up, Tenants effectively share the burden of vacancy with the Landlord. Tenants often negotiate caps or modifications to Gross-Up provisions; well-counseled Tenants always read for the specific gross-up rate.",
