        "REIT's first public-share Sale, converting private to listed structure.",
        "REIT IPOs follow general IPO mechanics but with REIT-specific disclosures: NAV per share, property roster, Hold Period assumptions, Cap Rate analysis, debt schedule. The 'roll-up' IPO consolidates multiple private funds into a single listed entity, often delivering liquidity to legacy LPs. Listed REITs trade at premiums or discounts to NAV based on management quality, growth pipeline, and sector outlook. Major US REIT IPOs of recent years: Cousins (2019 merger / spin), Equinix Asia (private to public via separate vehicle), several specialty REITs. The post-2020 IPO window was challenging; private alternatives (non-traded REIT, BDC structures) drew more capital.",
