        "A REIT or operating company distribution of a subsidiary's stock to existing shareholders — separating two businesses without a Sale.",
        "Distribution of a subsidiary's stock to existing shareholders, separating two businesses.",
        "REIT spin-offs unlock value where management of two businesses creates dis-synergy. Notable examples: Penn National's gaming Real Estate into GLPI (2013), Darden's Olive Garden Real Estate into Four Corners (2015), Marriott's Hotel real estate from operating businesses (multiple), Ryman Hospitality's spin-out from operations. Tax-free under IRC §355 if structured correctly — five-year operating-purpose requirement and other rules. Shareholders end up with stock in both the parent and the spin-off proportional to their parent holdings. The spin-off often outperforms the parent post-separation as separated focus drives execution.",
        ["IRS", "SEC", "Nareit"],
