        "Private acquisition of a listed REIT, removing it from public markets.",
        "Take-private transactions accelerated in 2020-2023 as listed REITs traded at discounts to private-market values. Notable deals: Blackstone's $13B take-private of American Campus Communities (2022), Blackstone + Starwood take-private of Extended Stay (2021), Brookfield's take-private of various asset-heavy REITs. Mechanics: cash tender offer typically 15-30% premium to undisturbed share price, board-and-shareholder approval, regulatory clearance. Once private, the REIT loses public-market liquidity but gains operational flexibility and avoids quarterly reporting pressure. The 2024 listed REIT recovery softened the take-private opportunity but didn't close it entirely.",
        ["SEC", "Nareit"],
