        "Bank guarantee of payment if specific conditions aren't met — secures Tenant performance.",
        "Commercial Tenants often post Letters of Credit in lieu of cash Security Deposits — the LOC ties up the Tenant's credit capacity but doesn't drain working capital. Lenders accept LOCs as collateral for environmental indemnification, completion guarantees, and Tenant Improvement reimbursement obligations. Cost to Tenant: 1-2% of face value annually as fees to the issuing bank. Sight LOCs pay on simple demand; standby LOCs require specific documentation. LOCs from investment-grade banks (BBB+ and above) are accepted broadly; LOCs from smaller banks may face additional scrutiny.",
